# Academy Layer Conventions

`academy/` holds video lessons. The catalog in `snippets/academy-lessons.js`
owns lesson order, titles, descriptions, and durations; `npm run sync-academy`
writes everything derived from it. Copy mechanics are in `help-mdx-copy.mdc`;
tone of voice in `.agents/skills/voice-review/tone.md`.

## Structure

```text
snippets/academy-lessons.js   # catalog: { slug, title, description, duration }
snippets/academy-grid.jsx     # <AcademyGrid lessons /> card grid
scripts/sync-academy.mjs      # generates the three outputs below
academy/index.mdx             # overview grid; lessons block between markers
academy/<slug>.mdx            # one lesson page per catalog entry
config/navigation/index.json  # Academy tab pages, rewritten by the script
academy.css                   # card outline and sidebar duration tag styling
```

## Patterns

Add or change a lesson:

1. Edit `snippets/academy-lessons.js`. `slug` is kebab-case and unique;
   `duration` is `m:ss` or `mm:ss`.
2. Run `npm run sync-academy`. It stubs a missing `academy/<slug>.mdx`,
   rewrites `title`, `description`, and `tag` in every lesson's frontmatter,
   regenerates the `academy-lessons:start` / `end` block in `academy/index.mdx`,
   and rewrites the Academy `pages` list.
3. Write the lesson body below the frontmatter: the video embed, then
   `## What you will learn` as three short bullets.

```js
{
  slug: 'sharing',
  title: 'Sharing a gallery',
  description: 'A short video about sharing a gallery.',
  duration: '2:47',
},
```

- Lesson pages use `mode: wide`. The `tag` field is the duration and renders
  as the sidebar time via `academy.css`.
- `npm run validate` runs `sync-academy --check` first and fails when the
  generated files are out of date.

## Boundaries

- Do not hand-edit the lessons block in `academy/index.mdx`, the `tag` field,
  or the Academy `pages` list. The next sync overwrites them.
- Do not remove the `academy-lessons:start` / `end` markers.
- Lesson bodies stay short: a video and what it covers. Step-by-step
  instructions belong in Guides; link there instead.
- `academy-grid.jsx` is layout only. Lesson data always arrives via props.
